# sqlite (player-realm metadata) + the pristine genesis snapshot
apps/web/data/

# audio — deliberately untracked, both the ~19MB of mp3 masters and the
# ~10MB of built Opus loops the app serves. Deploying them is an rsync, not
# a git pull; see deploy/README.md § "Audio assets".
#
# This is safe because nothing in the deploy path touches untracked files:
# no script runs `git clean`/`git reset --hard`, and `next build` never reads
# public/ (there's no `output: "standalone"`, so `next start` serves it live
# from disk). They survive `git pull` and rebuilds exactly the way
# apps/web/data/ does.
#
# A fresh clone therefore comes up silent, which the app handles — a missing
# file just fails to decode and nothing plays. Regenerate the loops from the
# masters with `pnpm --filter web audio:inspect --prepare-loops`, or get a
# usable dev soundtrack with no masters at all via `--placeholders`.
#
# The masters are the ONLY way to re-cut the loops. Back them up somewhere
# that isn't this working tree.
apps/web/assets-src/
apps/web/public/audio/

# generated deploy data: the address book written by scripts/sync-addresses.mjs
# and the three seeder caches. Committed templates live in
# apps/web/lib/contracts/defaults/ and are copied in by
# apps/web/scripts/ensure-generated.mjs, which every build/dev/test run calls.
# Untracked so a provisioned checkout keeps a clean worktree for `git pull`.
apps/web/lib/contracts/generated/
